  "question": {
    "text": "Let $S=\\left\\{p_1, p_2 \\ldots ., p_{10}\\right\\}$ be the set of first ten prime numbers. Let $A=S \\cup P$, where $P$ is the set of all possible products of distinct elements of $S$. Then the number of all ordered pairs ( $x, y$ ), $x \\in S$, $y \\in A$, such that $x$ divides $y$, is ______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5120",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\text { Let } \\frac{y}{x}=\\lambda \\\\ & y=\\lambda x \\\\ & =10 \\times\\left({ }^9 C_0+{ }^9 C_1+{ }^9 C_2+{ }^9 C_3+\\ldots+{ }^9 C_9\\right) \\\\ & =10 \\times 2 \\\\ & =10 \\times 512=5120\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
